// the allocation seam through a real link, and in a release build. three things only this can check:
// that the `linkonce_odr` thunks and the mutable counter survive being emitted into per-module objects
// and folded by the system linker, that the count is maintained with no debug build behind it - the flag
// is deliberately not tied to --debug - and that `main`'s report reaches a native binary's stdout
//
// the check is the report rather than an `assert`, and it has to be: `build` is a release build, so an
// assertion here would be compiled out and would assert nothing at all
//
// both halves of the seam are exercised: `Box` is the runtime's own block, `array<int32>` is the
// stdlib's raw buffer, and one counter sees both
class Box
{
    int32 $value;
}

{
    Box $b = Box(7);
    Box $c = $b;

    array<int32> $numbers = [1, 2];
    $numbers->push(3);

    echo $c->value;
    echo $numbers[2];
}
